>  Monk "Activate by Movement" was a very clever game tactics.
>  Traditionally, it is hard to give abilities to melee fighters.  Having
>  melee fighters select abilities from menus seems too much like what
>  wizards do.  Activate by Movement has the advantage of letting melee
>  fighters do what they do best - mash the direction arrows. [...]

What would be more convincing, and also a lot less trivial to perform,
(though of considerably less use when you want to take out Kaen in a
single move) would be to actually move around the dungeon in the
required directions, rather than just typing in the directions at the
prompt.

This is more along the lines of your reasoning about cloaks of
displacement being movement activated.  However, it is *more* like the
special moves of video games (which may indeed be something that puts
people off) because you can have the "fun" of performing a complex
series of moves while the enemy is attacking of you, only for it to
fail because you got one step wrong (rather than the one-step failure
"you stumble").

